 backend, compile an artifact, or initialize CUDA.
+
+## KernelBuildSpec v1
+
+`KernelBuildSpec` is the immutable, pointer-free identity input for one
+compiled region. `CompileRequest` supplies program/target policy; the build
+spec adds every region-level input that can change produced bytes:
+
+- SHA-256 digests of the canonical source/IR and callable ABI;
+- one `SemanticRoute`: `GenericDirect`, `StructuredTensorIr`, or
+  `ServingDirect` (serialized as `generic-direct`, `structured-tensorir`, or
+  `serving-direct`);
+- a full 40-character lowercase pipeline revision;
+- the complete resolved schedule;
+- SHA-256 digests of static specialization, symbolic specialization, argument
+  ABI, result ABI, and mutation ABI;
+- the parent `CompileRequest.byte_compile_identity_digest`;
+- optionally, one `CatalogProvenance` containing operator, problem, and
+  schedule SHA-256 digests together. The three catalog fields are all-or-none.
+
+The producer is responsible for canonicalizing and hashing source/IR,
+specializations, and ABI descriptions before construction. V1 validates every
+digest as 64 lowercase hexadecimal characters; it never reads or normalizes a
+framework object.
+
+### Generic resolved schedule
+
+`CanonicalSchedule` always carries eight explicit categories: `schedule`,
+`tile`, `layout`, `persistence`, `cta`, `warp`, `stage`, and `options`. Each is
+a strictly name-ordered list of at most 128 `ScheduleParameter` values. An
+empty category means explicitly inapplicable; it does not authorize an ambient
+default.
+
+A parameter name is a lowercase dotted identifier such as `cluster.x`.
+Parameters are typed scalars:
+
+| `ScheduleValueKind` | Canonical input spelling | MessagePack value |
+| ------------------- | ------------------------ | ----------------- |
+| `Boolean` | `false` or `true` | Boolean |
+| `SignedInteger` | minimal int64 decimal | Integer |
+| `UnsignedInteger` | minimal uint64 decimal | Integer |
+| `Text` | trimmed printable ASCII, 1 to 4096 bytes | String |
+
+Compound options are flattened into uniquely named scalar parameters. This
+keeps schedule identity generic and prevents a producer from hiding tile,
+layout, persistence, CTA, warp, stage, or other byte-affecting choices behind
+a process-local options object.
+
+```python
+from pypto.compiler import (
+    CanonicalSchedule,
+    KernelBuildSpec,
+    ScheduleParameter,
+    ScheduleValueKind,
+    SemanticRoute,
+)
+
+def u64(name: str, value: int) -> ScheduleParameter:
+    return ScheduleParameter(name, ScheduleValueKind.UnsignedInteger, str(value))
+
+
+resolved = CanonicalSchedule(
+    schedule=[ScheduleParameter("algorithm", ScheduleValueKind.Text, "blocked")],
+    tile=[u64("k", 64), u64("m", 128), u64("n", 128)],
+    layout=[ScheduleParameter("output", ScheduleValueKind.Text, "row-major")],
+    persistence=[ScheduleParameter("enabled", ScheduleValueKind.Boolean, "false")],
+    cta=[u64("threads", 256)],
+    warp=[u64("count", 8)],
+    stage=[u64("count", 3)],
+    options=[ScheduleParameter("fast_math", ScheduleValueKind.Boolean, "false")],
+)
+spec = KernelBuildSpec(
+    source_ir_digest="1" * 64,
+    callable_abi_digest="2" * 64,
+    semantic_route=SemanticRoute.GenericDirect,
+    pipeline_revision="3" * 40,
+    resolved_schedule=resolved,
+    static_specialization_digest="4" * 64,
+    symbolic_specialization_digest="5" * 64,
+    argument_abi_digest="6" * 64,
+    result_abi_digest="7" * 64,
+    mutation_abi_digest="8" * 64,
+    compile_request_byte_identity_digest="9" * 64,
+)
+wire_bytes = spec.serialize()
+assert KernelBuildSpec.deserialize(wire_bytes).serialize() == wire_bytes
+```
+
+`serialize()` emits canonical MessagePack and `identity_digest` is the
+lowercase SHA-256 of those complete bytes. `deserialize()` rejects malformed
+input, trailing bytes, missing/duplicate/unknown fields, unsupported versions
+or enums, noncanonical map/parameter order and noncanonical scalar encodings.
+The payload is capped at 1 MiB, with array, map, string, and nesting limits
+applied during MessagePack unpacking.
+
+The schema has no framework, model, or layer name; pointer, tensor, workspace,
+stream, or handle; produced bytes; or actual artifact kind. It performs no
+environment, filesystem, device, or backend query. This data-only contract
+does not link or invoke TensorIR/CUDA Tile, compile a region, create an
+artifact/cache/executable, modify runtime/plugins, or change legacy
+`ir.compile`.
